fix(web): CDP transport dropped messages with braces; token scrape picked wrong fields

The web channel never actually served a completion. Three independent defects,
each reproduced and measured; fixing only one or two leaves it broken.

1. WEBSOCKET FRAMING (the real reason everything looked hung)
   cdp.mjs never parsed the WebSocket wire format. It concatenated the raw
   stream and scanned for '{' … '}', counting brace depth to cut JSON objects.
   A CDP reply whose JSON *string value* contains braces — and Gemini's f.req
   responses are nested escaped JSON, so they contain thousands — desynchronises
   that counter. No message was ever cut, the pending promise never settled, and
   Runtime.evaluate waited forever.
   That is why token scrapes appeared to work (their replies carry no braces
   inside strings) while generation appeared to hang: same transport, different
   payload shape.
   Replaced with a real RFC 6455 reader: 7/16/64-bit length forms, masked-payload
   handling, continuation-frame reassembly, ping→pong, and close settling every
   pending call instead of leaving it hanging. The writer now also emits the
   64-bit length form for payloads >= 64KB; the old code fell into the 16-bit
   branch for everything >= 126 bytes and produced a header that lied.

2. SNlM0e COULD NOT MATCH A VALID TOKEN
   The token is "<22-char id>:<epoch millis>" and the pattern restricted it to
   [\w\-_], which excludes the colon. Every good page therefore raised
   "SNlM0e not found — session expired; run node bin/login.mjs" even though the
   session was fine. Now captured as the whole quoted string.

3. BUILD LABEL CAME FROM THE WRONG FIELD
   "FdrFJe" appears several times in the fetched HTML and the first hit is a bare
   number (measured: -7730566936813324387). The real label is the
   "boq_gemini-web-uiserver_20261029.22_p0" form. Sending the number did not
   fail loudly — StreamGenerate simply hung. scrapePageTokens now reads
   window.WIZ_global_data first (authoritative, and fresher than any re-fetched
   HTML because the SPA refreshes it in place), falling back to an HTML scrape
   whose build-label pattern is anchored on the boq_/prod- prefix.

Verified live after all three fixes, each account doing a real completion:
   pro1 zishuo391435@gmail.com   4729ms  16933 bytes  PONG
   pro2 wang391435@gmail.com     3488ms  16957 bytes  PONG
   pro3 zishuowang35@gmail.com   4578ms  16932 bytes  PONG

Tests: +15 (cdp.test.mjs pins the framing invariants and both length forms;
session-tokens.test.mjs pins the token patterns and the request shape).
Suite 107/107 green.

Also adds the probes that produced this evidence: matrix-test (account x model),
probe-project-sharing (per-account quota vs shared project), probe-quota-raw
(5h/weekly buckets), verify-unlock-proxy (region-field stripping through the
mitmproxy addon), verify-one-web (single-account end-to-end), extract-cookies
(DPAPI cookie decrypt, documents why cookie copying cannot work).
